# Small local model compatibility

goclaw targets **qwen2.5-coder:7b** (7B, ~8K–32K effective context). Every prompt addition must be constrained.

## Context injection limits (do not exceed)

| Source | Limit | Config key |
|--------|-------|------------|
| Skills snippet | `EffectiveSkillsMaxRunes()` default 8 000 | `skills_max_runes` |
| Memory entries per store | `EffectiveMaxMemorySnippetEntries()` default 4 | `max_memory_snippet_entries` |
| Each memory block | 4 096 bytes | — |
| Plan body in multi-step | 30 lines | — |
| MCP tools in prompt | 0 (hidden by default) | — |

## Required

- **Every new injection** must have a size cap with a truncation note on cut.
- **Caps must use `EffectiveXxx()`** methods — never hard-code a number at the call site.
- **MCP tools** register via `reg.AddHidden`, not `reg.Register`.
- **Multi-step plans**: use `StepExecutionUserMessages`; do not re-inject the full plan body.
- **Tool list size**: keep visible tools ≤ ~15 per turn; rely on `tool_search` for the rest.

## Forbidden

```go
// WRONG — uncapped file content in system prompt
sys += "\n## File\n" + entireFileContent

// WRONG — all MCP tools always visible
reg.Register(mcpAdapter) // use reg.AddHidden instead

// WRONG — hard-coded limit at call site
skills.Collect(roots, 24000)  // use cfg.EffectiveSkillsMaxRunes()
```

## Qwen-specific note

`qwenFamily()` check in `request.go` appends a numbered-steps suffix. Keep model-specific hacks in `request.go` only — not in tools or plan files.
